Yphtach and Lucy,

This issue you identified in logit.mixed is now fixed in the Beta versions.  Sorry for the delay as we have just now gotten to the ZeligMultilevel module.  Below is a slight modification of the example that Yphtach proposed, which now works.  Note that the code is installing from the r.iq repository to get the current Betas.  (Lucy, if your issue was different, and you still have any issues, feel free to let me know on or off list).



# Yphtach's example:


install.packages("Zelig", type = "source", repos = "http://r.iq.harvard.edu/")

install.packages("ZeligMultilevel", type = "source", repos = "http://r.iq.harvard.edu/")


library(Zelig)

library(ZeligMultilevel)


d <- expand.grid(y=rbinom(10,1,.33),x=rnorm(10,1),t=1:4)

z.out <- zelig(y~x+tag(1|t),data=d,model="logit.mixed")

x.out<-setx(z.out)

s.out<-sim(z.out, x=x.out)

plot(s.out)


